WEBVTT

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:10.240
I can't finish reading the magazine pages

00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:17.150
I get the feeling that I must read it

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:23.900
Game cartridges are stacked in the corner of the room

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:30.600
Is there no meaning if I don't play them?

00:00:32.830 --> 00:00:35.700
You're on the other side of the table

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:39.070
I'm talking to you, but...

00:00:39.670 --> 00:00:46.000
You don't change your facial expression at all

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:52.250
Even though I'm this close to you

00:00:52.750 --> 00:00:59.520
These feelings don't reach you, don't reach you

00:00:59.940 --> 00:01:06.260
What is truly precious?

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:15.950
Mysterious Transfer Student  Ryuji Otogi

00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:23.160
Grandpa, I'm leaving.

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:23.900
Okay.

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.260
Grandpa?

00:01:27.260 --> 00:01:28.750
Good morning, Yugi.

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:30.770
Good morning, Anzu.

00:01:30.770 --> 00:01:32.710
Good morning, Grandpa.

00:01:32.710 --> 00:01:33.620
Yeah...

00:01:34.970 --> 00:01:36.780
What's wrong, Yugi?

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:39.310
Your grandpa seems to be in a bad mood.

00:01:39.310 --> 00:01:43.060
Just between us, Grandpa is down in the dumps.

00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.000
Why?

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.840
I'm glad you asked!

00:01:47.080 --> 00:01:51.790
In my seventy-two years of life, Sugoroku Muto has never been in such a pinch!

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:56.590
My store may go out of business!

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.660
Look at that!

00:01:58.660 --> 00:02:00.870
A new game shop?

00:02:00.870 --> 00:02:05.520
Yes.  They're acquiring and selling the best games from around the world.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:10.980
And it seems they'll be selling a new game as their featured product.

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:12.940
A new game?

00:02:12.940 --> 00:02:15.700
Sorry Grandpa, but that piques my curiosity.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:16.780
How dare you!

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.370
Anzu, let's check it out!

00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:20.640
Wait up!

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:25.240
Here.

00:02:25.350 --> 00:02:26.330
Thanks.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:31.380
What kind of game is DDM?

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:32.560
C'mon, Yugi!

00:02:32.690 --> 00:02:34.370
We'll be late for school.

00:02:37.170 --> 00:02:40.740
That's Yugi Muto, Otogi.

00:02:42.880 --> 00:02:44.380
That little kid?

00:02:44.380 --> 00:02:48.510
Yeah.  They say no can beat him at Duel Monsters.

00:02:48.510 --> 00:02:52.560
In Duelist Kingdom, he defeated Pegasus and won the championship.

00:02:53.050 --> 00:03:01.800
But the Duel Monsters champ may not take on DDM - Dungeon Dice Monsters.

00:03:01.800 --> 00:03:03.000
No problem.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:07.260
Just watch.  I'll take everything dear to him one by one.

00:03:07.420 --> 00:03:11.820
I promise to drag him on to the DDM battlefield.

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:13.220
You're full of spirit.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:16.940
Is promoting DDM really your only purpose?

00:03:17.240 --> 00:03:19.940
Don't pry into my business.

00:03:19.940 --> 00:03:26.380
When I defeat Yugi and increase the appeal of DDM around the world, that should make you happy.

00:03:26.380 --> 00:03:27.760
Ooh, scary.

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.760
Don't get angry, Otogi.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:33.770
Yugi Muto, I promise to defeat you.

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:38.470
I will avenge him by taking your title as the King of Games.

00:03:42.200 --> 00:03:44.740
Oh, a new game shop?

00:03:44.960 --> 00:03:47.220
Grandpa is depressed.

00:03:47.220 --> 00:03:50.200
His store now has strong competition.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:54.760
They're going to sell a new game called DDM.

00:03:54.760 --> 00:03:57.500
You mean Dungeon Dice Monsters?

00:03:57.730 --> 00:04:00.330
How do you know so much?

00:04:00.330 --> 00:04:03.740
There was an advertisement in the newspaper this morning.

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.270
What?  You read the newspaper, Jonouchi?

00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.490
I saw it while I was delivering newspapers!

00:04:09.850 --> 00:04:11.600
Having a job is against the rules.

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:13.640
You're one to talk!

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:17.320
I received special permission so that I could pay school expenses.

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:21.810
I'm saving the money prize that Yugi gave me for Shizuka's operation.

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:24.220
So Shizuka is getting the operation?

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:29.540
Yeah.  The specialist said that the operation will completely restore her eyesight.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.500
That's great, Jonouchi!

00:04:31.500 --> 00:04:32.250
Yeah!

00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:40.900
What's going on?

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:44.920
Do it again!

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:45.850
Sure.

00:04:45.850 --> 00:04:47.820
I'll use six dice this time.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:53.740
Here I go.

00:05:06.400 --> 00:05:08.270
Who is he?

00:05:08.550 --> 00:05:11.600
Hey, is he in your class?

00:05:12.280 --> 00:05:15.860
That's Ryuji Otogi.  He transferred here yesterday.

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.720
Now you know.

00:05:17.720 --> 00:05:23.720
I can't stand guys who show off to attract girls.

00:05:24.250 --> 00:05:27.570
You don't like any guy who's popular with girls.

00:05:28.540 --> 00:05:34.480
I'm the type who sheathes his sharpened sword.

00:05:34.480 --> 00:05:38.700
I don't brag about my talents!

00:05:38.700 --> 00:05:41.120
You have talents?

00:05:43.850 --> 00:05:47.580
Didn't you see anything while we were at Duelist Kingdom?

00:05:47.580 --> 00:05:49.900
They say that luck is a part of skill.

00:05:49.900 --> 00:05:50.960
What did you say?

00:05:50.960 --> 00:05:52.600
Knock it off, you two.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:56.520
I became aware of my talents on that island.

00:05:56.840 --> 00:05:59.260
My talents as a duelist!

00:06:00.980 --> 00:06:04.140
So you're talented at Duel Monsters?

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:13.080
I bet you heard of Keith Howard, the invincible former American champion.

00:06:13.320 --> 00:06:17.420
He played well, but he was no match for me.

00:06:17.420 --> 00:06:19.150
Now who's showing off?

00:06:19.150 --> 00:06:21.330
His sword is unsheathed.

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:23.610
Do you now know how great I am?

00:06:23.850 --> 00:06:27.860
Aren't you Duelist Kingdom champion Yugi Muto?

00:06:28.000 --> 00:06:29.260
Yeah.

00:06:29.260 --> 00:06:31.950
I've heard stories about your accomplishments.

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:35.420
And stories about second place Katsuya Jonouchi?

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:37.620
Sorry.

00:06:37.620 --> 00:06:41.980
Let's play a game, and you can show me how talented you are.

00:06:42.170 --> 00:06:43.680
A game?

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:44.610
Yes.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:46.980
We'll use this die and a cup.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:49.920
A game?  What does he have in mind?

00:06:50.480 --> 00:06:52.320
Do your best!

00:06:53.460 --> 00:06:57.110
If I defeat Otogi, all his fans will belong to me.

00:06:57.510 --> 00:06:59.300
Fine, I'll do it.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:01.420
Then watch closely.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:12.730
I can move the die to my right hand without touching the cup.

00:07:12.730 --> 00:07:14.810
That's impossible.

00:07:15.060 --> 00:07:19.930
Unless you have ESP, you can't make the die teleport.

00:07:20.830 --> 00:07:24.540
While you were talking, the die vanished from underneath the cup.

00:07:24.540 --> 00:07:25.550
What?

00:07:25.650 --> 00:07:27.070
Do you think I'm lying?

00:07:27.070 --> 00:07:29.130
Then see for yourself.

00:07:29.460 --> 00:07:30.430
That's ridiculous.

00:07:31.370 --> 00:07:33.180
It's a trap, Jonouchi!

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.110
The die is right there.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:42.640
I moved the die into my right hand without touching the cup.

00:07:42.930 --> 00:07:44.070
I win.

00:07:45.540 --> 00:07:47.300
Stop messing around!

00:07:47.300 --> 00:07:51.200
I won't let this lame game decide a winner and a loser!

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:53.750
Battle me fair and square in Duel Monsters!

00:07:54.020 --> 00:07:55.310
Fine.

00:07:55.310 --> 00:07:59.420
But since you're an expert at this game, I have one condition.

00:07:59.420 --> 00:08:00.520
Condition?

00:08:00.520 --> 00:08:01.300
Fine.

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:02.860
I accept any condition.

00:08:03.750 --> 00:08:06.510
I don't have a deck of my own.

00:08:07.220 --> 00:08:08.940
That's not fair!

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:12.100
Fine.  So what do you want to do?

00:08:12.490 --> 00:08:17.900
In our duel, we'll open brand new packs and create our decks on the spot.

00:08:17.900 --> 00:08:20.280
That's a fair condition, right?

00:08:20.830 --> 00:08:22.260
That's crazy!

00:08:22.260 --> 00:08:25.580
If you don't play with your usual cards, luck plays a huge role.

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:29.080
There are a lot of cards that Jonouchi doesn't know.

00:08:29.080 --> 00:08:31.020
Don't worry, Yugi.

00:08:31.020 --> 00:08:34.960
Do you doubt my skills when I dueled for the right to challenge Pegasus?

00:08:35.120 --> 00:08:36.760
That's not what I mean.

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.940
I accept your condition.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:39.930
Jonouchi!

00:08:39.930 --> 00:08:43.710
And just playing a game for fun is boring.

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:47.980
If you lose, you have to do whatever I say for a week.

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:50.120
How interesting.

00:08:50.120 --> 00:08:55.280
But if I win, all your girls will have to become my fans.

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:58.510
What?  No way!  You're the worst!

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.740
Be quiet!

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:01.950
Stay out of a battle between men!

00:09:01.950 --> 00:09:03.100
Idiot.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.240
This isn't good.

00:09:04.240 --> 00:09:06.520
Jonouchi, you shouldn't do this.

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:10.890
Yugi, do you think I'll lose to this stuck-up punk?

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:16.300
Do you think I haven't improved since finishing in the top eight in the regionals?

00:09:16.300 --> 00:09:18.000
That's not what I mean.

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:19.570
Then be quiet!

00:09:20.200 --> 00:09:26.650
We'll have the match after school in the new game shop's Duel Ring.

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:27.510
All right?

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:28.540
Sure.

00:09:28.740 --> 00:09:32.680
You should come watch your friend's awesome duel.

00:09:33.450 --> 00:09:37.540
Otogi...  I wonder what he's thinking.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:43.760
I'm marching into enemy territory!

00:09:43.760 --> 00:09:45.480
I'll take him down!

00:09:48.620 --> 00:09:51.380
Will Jonouchi be okay?

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:54.640
When that idiot is on an ego trip, no one can stop him.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:57.810
I hope he doesn't get humiliated.

00:09:58.080 --> 00:09:59.970
Welcome!

00:09:59.970 --> 00:10:02.350
So you're Otogi's opponent.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:03.480
Come this way.

00:10:05.940 --> 00:10:07.150
You arrived.

00:10:07.410 --> 00:10:09.500
The Duel Ring is below.

00:10:09.500 --> 00:10:10.590
Get in.

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.520
Choose whatever packs you like.

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:17.220
Use these new cards to build your deck.

00:10:17.220 --> 00:10:18.960
Yeah, I know.

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:28.110
All right!  Choosing powerful cards is also my talent!

00:10:28.490 --> 00:10:30.290
How'd it go, Jonouchi?

00:10:30.290 --> 00:10:32.820
Don't worry!  I'm going to win!

00:10:52.260 --> 00:10:54.570
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:10:54.570 --> 00:10:56.920
Let's go!  Let's go, Otogi!

00:10:56.920 --> 00:10:57.830
What's this?

00:10:59.620 --> 00:11:02.020
Hooray hooray Otogi!

00:11:02.020 --> 00:11:03.270
L-O-V-E Otogi!

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.340
It's the same Ring as Kaiba Land.

00:11:05.340 --> 00:11:07.580
It's a rental.  And expensive.

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:10.480
What are the cameras for?

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:14.750
A duel is more exciting when more people watch.

00:11:16.050 --> 00:11:18.850
This duel will be webcast worldwide.

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:25.790
Duelists around the world can watch the Duelist Kingdom's runner-up lose.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.220
How naïve.

00:11:28.220 --> 00:11:30.660
Listen, Otogi.  I'm going to win!

00:11:30.660 --> 00:11:34.840
Then those Otogi girls will become Jonouchi girls!

00:11:34.970 --> 00:11:37.270
No way!  You're the worst!

00:11:37.510 --> 00:11:38.780
Don't worry.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.110
I'll protect you.

00:11:42.080 --> 00:11:44.600
You're so cool!  You're great!

00:11:45.710 --> 00:11:47.050
Be quiet!

00:11:47.320 --> 00:11:47.920
Damn!

00:11:54.680 --> 00:11:56.240
I'm ready.

00:11:56.240 --> 00:11:57.530
Let's start this duel.

00:11:58.060 --> 00:11:59.180
You can go first.

00:12:05.310 --> 00:12:07.570
L-O-V-E Otogi!

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:08.940
Duel!

00:12:09.340 --> 00:12:10.770
It's my turn.

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:15.290
Oni Tank T-34 in attack position!

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:19.900
That ends my turn.

00:12:19.900 --> 00:12:23.590
Show me your dueling talent, Jonouchi.

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:25.390
You don't need to ask.

00:12:28.270 --> 00:12:31.090
What's this?  It's a card with a powerful effect!

00:12:31.790 --> 00:12:34.530
It can equip monsters that it destroys.

00:12:35.080 --> 00:12:35.970
All right!

00:12:36.610 --> 00:12:38.900
Sword Hunter in attack position!

00:12:39.270 --> 00:12:40.300
Battle!

00:12:40.300 --> 00:12:41.810
Hunter's Chance!

00:12:47.350 --> 00:12:48.460
All right!

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:49.860
Oni Tank is destroyed!

00:12:51.950 --> 00:12:59.110
Oni Tank is equipped on to Sword Hunter, raising its attack points by 200!

00:12:59.950 --> 00:13:02.810
No no Otogi!

00:13:02.810 --> 00:13:05.900
Jonouchi is doing pretty well.

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:07.210
Right, Yugi?

00:13:07.210 --> 00:13:07.780
Yeah...

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:09.500
How's that, Otogi?

00:13:09.500 --> 00:13:12.440
An amateur like you was never a match for me.

00:13:12.610 --> 00:13:14.470
Impressive, Jonouchi.

00:13:15.590 --> 00:13:18.440
It's too late for you to realize that.

00:13:18.440 --> 00:13:19.970
C'mon.  It's your turn.

00:13:26.170 --> 00:13:27.950
Dark Bat in defense position.

00:13:28.830 --> 00:13:31.330
Then I set one card.

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:38.240
Well, I won't let you survive by playing defense.

00:13:40.280 --> 00:13:43.100
Mad Sword Beast in attack position!

00:13:43.840 --> 00:13:45.100
Let's battle!

00:13:55.030 --> 00:13:57.830
I'm glad I played it in defense position.

00:13:58.600 --> 00:14:05.360
Even if your monster is in defense position, Mad Sword Beast breaks through and deals you damage.

00:14:06.960 --> 00:14:09.030
You're incredible, Jonouchi.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:13.260
But my monster doesn't want to go to the graveyard on its own.

00:14:13.640 --> 00:14:14.590
Too bad.

00:14:14.590 --> 00:14:15.400
What?

00:14:24.140 --> 00:14:26.600
Jonouchi's strategy is too simple.

00:14:26.600 --> 00:14:28.440
Don't let your guard down, Jonouchi!

00:14:28.600 --> 00:14:31.450
I did that on purpose to make the game more interesting.

00:14:32.060 --> 00:14:34.750
I can beat this guy in my sleep.

00:14:35.320 --> 00:14:39.810
Otogi appears to be in a tight spot, but he's actually controlling the game.

00:14:39.810 --> 00:14:41.690
Be careful, Jonouchi.

00:14:41.960 --> 00:14:44.400
That was a cheap trick you pulled.

00:14:44.400 --> 00:14:46.730
But I still have the advantage!

00:14:46.730 --> 00:14:53.200
Now that your formidable monster is gone, it's time for my counterattack.

00:14:54.720 --> 00:14:56.960
I set one card.

00:14:58.000 --> 00:15:01.540
Next, I summon Spikebot!

00:15:02.820 --> 00:15:03.940
Battle!

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:09.850
Try harder, Jonouchi!

00:15:09.850 --> 00:15:13.600
This isn't "The Tortoise and the Hare," so stop snoozing!

00:15:13.600 --> 00:15:17.190
If you lose, you have to do whatever Otogi says!

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:19.550
Oh yeah!

00:15:19.550 --> 00:15:21.330
I'll start playing seriously.

00:15:22.730 --> 00:15:23.920
All right!

00:15:23.920 --> 00:15:27.400
This super powerful card will trounce your monster!

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:28.690
Go!

00:15:35.000 --> 00:15:39.450
Otogi, you barely have any life points left!

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.320
Otogi, oh no!

00:15:42.500 --> 00:15:47.550
Their weakness is that after they attack, they're stuck in defense position until the next turn.

00:15:47.900 --> 00:15:50.820
But Otogi only has 50 life points left.

00:15:51.480 --> 00:15:53.240
I'm guaranteed to win!

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:56.060
Prepare yourselves, Jonouchi girls!

00:15:56.060 --> 00:16:00.170
No!  Hang in there, Otogi!

00:16:00.930 --> 00:16:05.080
I don't like the idea of Jonouchi girls, but he's dueling great!

00:16:05.080 --> 00:16:07.110
Yeah!  You're going to win!

00:16:07.620 --> 00:16:12.550
Why is Otogi so calm when he hardly has any life points left?

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:15.390
Does he have a secret strategy?

00:16:15.860 --> 00:16:19.880
Jonouchi, don't let your guard down!  The duel is only getting started!

00:16:17.450 --> 00:16:20.460
The outcome is already determined.

00:16:20.460 --> 00:16:22.880
Hooray hooray Jonouchi!

00:16:23.580 --> 00:16:24.730
It's no good.

00:16:24.910 --> 00:16:26.360
It's my turn.

00:16:26.660 --> 00:16:30.730
I summon Gradius in attack position!

00:16:34.610 --> 00:16:37.020
That doesn't worry me at all.

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:41.140
The spell card Limiter Removal.

00:16:41.520 --> 00:16:43.970
It powers up Gradius!

00:16:46.240 --> 00:16:48.300
2400 attack points?

00:16:48.300 --> 00:16:50.400
I'm glad I have my Goblins.

00:16:50.430 --> 00:16:52.520
He could've beaten me in one strike.

00:16:52.520 --> 00:16:56.490
I activate the Equip Spell Fairy Meteor Crush!

00:16:57.330 --> 00:16:58.370
What?

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.390
Uh, what effect does that card have?

00:17:02.390 --> 00:17:06.550
You made it to second place without even knowing that?

00:17:06.550 --> 00:17:11.220
It's like a spell card version of your Mad Sword Beast.

00:17:11.220 --> 00:17:12.400
I see.

00:17:12.710 --> 00:17:14.070
That means...

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:16.710
When attacking a monster in defense position...

00:17:16.710 --> 00:17:22.710
...if my equipped monster has more attack points than your monster's defense points...

00:17:22.710 --> 00:17:26.650
...the difference is dealt to you as damage!

00:17:26.650 --> 00:17:27.770
What?

00:17:27.980 --> 00:17:29.590
Gradius, attack!

00:17:46.940 --> 00:17:48.960
You did it!

00:17:48.960 --> 00:17:50.440
I told you so!

00:17:50.440 --> 00:17:52.880
Jonouchi, you got carried away.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.150
Thank goodness!

00:17:58.410 --> 00:17:58.990
Here.

00:18:00.010 --> 00:18:03.260
Jonouchi, you must keep your promise.

00:18:03.260 --> 00:18:06.830
You'll be my pet dog for a week.

00:18:08.410 --> 00:18:14.540
During Duelist Kingdom, I was able to try harder than usual because I had an important goal.

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:17.770
But after accomplishing my goal, I've become overconfident.

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:19.860
That's enough!

00:18:19.860 --> 00:18:22.450
It's not funny anymore!

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:24.530
Yugi, stay out of this.

00:18:24.530 --> 00:18:25.720
This is my problem.

00:18:28.170 --> 00:18:29.680
Ouch!

00:18:30.340 --> 00:18:31.400
Jonouchi!

00:18:31.400 --> 00:18:33.070
Don't talk!

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:34.190
You're a dog!

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:36.260
Don't talk to anyone but me!

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:37.770
Come on!

00:18:37.770 --> 00:18:39.730
Okay, I promise.

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.480
Ouch...

00:18:44.480 --> 00:18:46.450
Not “ouch.”  Say “woof.”

00:18:48.560 --> 00:18:51.570
Wear that costume and bark.

00:18:54.680 --> 00:18:55.860
Do it.

00:19:01.850 --> 00:19:04.520
It suits you quite well.

00:19:07.180 --> 00:19:08.490
Woof!

00:19:10.780 --> 00:19:12.180
You're really good.

00:19:12.180 --> 00:19:13.500
Jonouchi...

00:19:19.770 --> 00:19:24.170
Otogi, you have some nerve for picking on my friend right in front of me!

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:27.220
I'll face you!

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:29.650
If I win, you let Jonouchi go!

00:19:29.790 --> 00:19:31.100
Fine.

00:19:31.100 --> 00:19:33.550
But we'll play a different game.

00:19:33.760 --> 00:19:38.090
You'll face me in DDM - Dungeon Dice Monsters!

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:39.100
What?

00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:42.890
If you lose, you'll relinquish your title as the King of Games.

00:19:43.160 --> 00:19:47.600
And you must vow never to play Duel Monsters again.

00:19:48.250 --> 00:19:50.040
That's going too far!

00:19:50.040 --> 00:19:51.160
Don't do it, Yugi!

00:19:51.160 --> 00:19:53.480
Jonouchi is paying for his own mistakes.

00:19:53.480 --> 00:19:55.100
That's right!  Don't accept, Yugi!

00:20:01.310 --> 00:20:03.320
Listen closely!

00:20:03.320 --> 00:20:05.850
Your game can't break our friendship!

00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:08.850
I accept your DDM match!

00:20:31.880 --> 00:20:33.350
That's crazy, Yugi!

00:20:33.350 --> 00:20:37.550
You accepted Otogi's challenge when you never played DDM before?

00:20:37.550 --> 00:20:42.620
He even made you promise never to play Duel Monsters again if you lose!

00:20:42.750 --> 00:20:47.080
While Yugi has trouble understanding the game, Otogi deals a one-sided attack.

00:20:47.280 --> 00:20:50.730
Why is he so hostile towards Yugi?

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:52.480
There must be a reason why.

00:20:52.770 --> 00:20:56.350
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Showdown!
Dungeon Dice Monsters

00:20:56.350 --> 00:20:57.820
Duel, standby!

00:21:02.050 --> 00:21:10.450
The flask glistens

00:21:11.490 --> 00:21:18.300
Wait for me in the science classroom

00:21:18.790 --> 00:21:27.270
If we put our cold hands together

00:21:27.980 --> 00:21:35.050
And rub them together, they become warm

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:40.880
Shower of happiness

00:21:41.170 --> 00:21:44.990
I will shower you with it

00:21:45.320 --> 00:21:53.270
I will support you even when you feel lonely

00:21:53.470 --> 00:21:57.500
Shower of happiness

00:21:57.770 --> 00:22:01.630
You are not alone

00:22:02.010 --> 00:22:08.350
You're protected by a giant ring of friendship
